## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of private AWS data access patterns, policy composition, and practical testing. 

## Key Concepts
- S3 public access blocking and bucket policy conditions
- VPC Endpoints and endpoint policies
- aws:SourceVpce condition and VPCE validation
- IAM roles for data producers

## Code Example
```
# Bucket policy (allow via VPCE)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": "*",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject","s3:PutObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::landing-logs/*",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"aws:SourceVpce": "vpce-abc123"}}
    }
  ]
}
```
```
# VPCE policy (minimal, allows basic access to bucket)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject","s3:PutObject"],
      "Resource": ["arn:aws:s3:::landing-logs/*"]
    }
  ]
}
```
```
# IAM role for producer (trusts producer principal)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {"Effect": "Allow","Action": ["s3:PutObject"],"Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::landing-logs/*"}
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale this to multiple VPCEs per environment?
- How would you monitor and audit VPCE access over time?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design idempotent, serverless onboarding with minimal IAM surface, a common beginner-safe pattern.

## Key Concepts
- Idempotent operations; DynamoDB conditional/transactional writes
- Least-privilege IAM for Lambda
- CloudWatch metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Node.js Lambda outline for idempotent signup
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const ddb = new AWS.DynamoDB.DocumentClient();
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const { userId, email, transactionId } = JSON.parse(event.body);
  const params = {
    TransactItems: [
      {
        Put: {
          TableName: 'Signups',
          Item: { userId, email, signupAt: Date.now() },
          ConditionExpression: 'attribute_not_exists(userId)'
        }
      },
      {
        Put: {
          TableName: 'SignupsDedup',
          Item: { transactionId, userId },
          ConditionExpression: 'attribute_not_exists(transactionId)'
        }
      }
    ]
  };
  await ddb.transactWrite(params).promise();
  return { statusCode: 200, body: JSON.stringify({ success: true }) };
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle cold starts or retries that occur during a transaction?
- How would you test this in a CI/CD pipeline and observe idempotent behavior?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design cross-region, multi-account DR with strict IAM boundaries and automated failover.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-region replication (S3 CRR, DynamoDB Global Tables)
- Route 53 failover with health checks
- Per-tenant IAM roles with least privilege and explicit denies
- IaC automation and DR testing

## Code Example

```terraform
# Minimal Terraform snippet for Route53 failover
resource "aws_route53_health_check" "region_a" {
  fqdn = "api.example.com"
  type = "HTTPS"
}

resource "aws_route53_record" "primary" {
  name = "api.example.com"
  type = "A"
  zone_id = var.zone_id
  set_identifier = "RegionA"
  failover_routing_policy {
    type = "primary"
    health_check_id = aws_route53_health_check.region_a.id
  }
  alias {
    name = aws_lb.region_a.dns_name
    zone_id = aws_lb.region_a.zone_id
  }
}

resource "aws_route53_record" "secondary" {
  name = "api.example.com"
  type = "A"
  zone_id = var.zone_id
  set_identifier = "RegionB"
  failover_routing_policy {
    type = "secondary"
    health_check_id = aws_route53_health_check.region_b.id
  }
  alias {
    name = aws_lb.region_b.dns_name
    zone_id = aws_lb.region_b.zone_id
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you verify data consistency after failover?
- What monitoring alerts would you add?

Why This Is Asked

This question probes tenancy boundaries across AWS accounts and how to enforce data residency and least-privilege access in a scalable, automated way.

Key Concepts

- Cross-account AssumeRole and STS
- Per-tenant S3 + CMK in tenant accounts
- Least-privilege IAM roles and bucket policies
- Data residency, rotation, and auditability
- DR/backup and cross-region considerations

Code Example

```javascript
